{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user ran `/goal`: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\" A Stop hook blocks stopping until met.\n   - STAGE.md: build the game in TASK.md following PLAN.md (by claude-opus-5-5 max) using its title (\"Big Buck Hunt-Off\"); where they disagree TASK.md wins (file names use `claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050516`, date 2026-11-04 05:05:16).\n   - TASK.md requirements: original game inspired by Big Buck Hunter Pro; single HTML `BigBuckHuntOff-BigBuckHunterPro-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050516.html` in work root; dev subfolder same name; built on my-3d2dge handoff (engine may be changed); engine native art/animation; all audio in code, Animalese gibberish voices; AI Hub lib/hub multiplayer (and works standalone); feature-complete polished vertical slice; dev mode from pause menu with live sliders + reset to defaults; attract mode after 10 s idle on title/menu, any input exits; 10-foot controller-first UI (DualSense/standard pad, PS glyphs default with Xbox setting option, KB+M native, mouse aims/hover focuses, prompts follow last device), no dense web screens; touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\", settings button, attract runs; no TODOs/placeholders/stubs; Source Information + Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback in chat reply AND in-game About/Credits; exit-interview.json in exact shape (sourceInformation 15 fields; testingFeedback 4; engineFeedback 6; promptFeedback 4; aiHub {name, tagline, description, type, genre, source, series, players, controls, tags 3-6}); \"unknown\" where unconfirmed. Source info fields: Date 2026-11-04 05:05:16; Environment \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\"; Model \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\"; Usage estimate only if available.\n   - Feedback questions: Testing: How many issues did testing catch? How many critical/game breaking? Most helpful test? Least helpful test? Engine: What did you like most? Did you get stuck or guess wrong? Most important thing you had to build yourself? Hardest part of using the engine? What did you change in the engine, and why? If you could change one thing? Prompt: What did you like most? What was confusing? Hardest thing? What would you change?\n   - Constraints (verbatim from TASK.md): \"Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\" \"Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\" Use TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp (/tmp nearly full).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (fixed 1/120 s steps, scenes, E.Shell HTML menus, settings, input presets must include start/pause/confirm/cancel, E.Dialog, E.Arcade tables/initials, game.saves (memory-only headless), E.store, E.Script steppable via `_step(dt)`, Backdrop layers, View projection ax/ay/bx/by/bz).\n   - Custom pseudo-3D voxel landscape renderer (column march front-to-back, per-column occlusion breakpoints occD/occY, billboards far→near composited into Uint32 frame, impostor sprite levels, crop layer for corn/reeds, canopy-as-terrain beyond 150 m, fog/mist, water, LUT grade, scope as magnified lens re-render).\n   - Off-axis perspective Lens (verticals vertical); project/ray/magnified/angles/fromAngles; setupLens shared by update and draw (WYSIWYG + determinism).\n   - Procedural Quadruped rigs with planted hooves, IK legs, poses, death roll; hit zones from same joints (spheres, capsules, ellipsoids); analytic shot rays; ~0.7 px forgiveness pad.\n   - Deterministic RNG streams (world/spawn/ai/bot/fx); no Math.random; site scripts on site clock; time-boxed sites use time-only spawn conditions.\n   - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 ghost mode: own card, ready() once, 3:00 timeline keyed to AIHub.time(), progress 1/s, one result, ghosts ≤10/s unreliable, shots reliable, end handling.\n   - Headless vm test loader; parallel test runner; Playwright browser checks.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (dev folder root: /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050516__x4cdb93/work/BigBuckHuntOff-BigBuckHunterPro-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050516/):\n   - vendor/engine-src (clone, sparse dist/handoff), vendor/hub-src (lib/hub); hub/session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js copied; tools/check.mjs, filmstrip.mjs copied; package.json with playwright 1.63.0 (Chromium 1243 cached).\n   - engine/my-3d2dge.js: changes — `glyphs ... value: 'playstation'`; `_settingsRows` filters `!S.spec(k).hidden`; `_render` adds `if (s.rows) for (const k of v(s.rows)) { if '#'.. section heading else add(this._row(k)) }`; non-std own items skip hidden; `bus(name = 'sfx')` on ChipAudio.\n   - engine/modules/vista.js, quadruped.js, babble.js (described above). Recent quadruped zones() additions: second head capsule skull→muzzle; neck as two capsules (neck→neckMid r≈neckR0*.9, neckMid→headBase r=(r0+r1)/2*.9); per-section ellipsoids `{ id: region(x), kind: 'ell', c, ax:[F.f,F.r,F.u], rad:[gap*(end?.3:.62)*scale, hw*.98*scale, (top-bot)/2*.98*scale] }` plus mid-section ellipsoids, z.a=z.c, z.r=max(rad); legs top→mid (legR[0]*1.2), mid→knee, knee→fet (legR[2]*1.1), fet→hoof (legR[3]*1.15); ears via `_earPts()` (r earW*.75, id head) and tail via `_tailPts()` (id ham); W scales offsets by scale about rig root; gut capsule end at sec[3][0]+4.5.\n   - src/42-shot.js: `function rayZones(o, d, zones, pad = 0)` (spheres r+pad, ell rad+pad, capsules r+pad); in resolveRay: `const hits = rayZones(ray, ray, a.zones(), .7 * Math.max(1, D) / H.lens.f);`; shared kill via `a.killStep`.\n   - src/11-props.js: added `rayEllipsoid(o, d, c, ax, rad)`; 'lowberm' prop; snag thinner/lighter.\n   - src/30-actors.js: `snapRig()` (reset legs planted, rig.update(0,...)) called in constructor; hearCall checks trophy rules first (even when hidden); trophy wounded hook.\n   - src/32-site.js: `this.script = new E.Script(G.game, function* () { yield* def.script(S); })` stepped in update when phase==='play'; reloopAt timing; timeBoxed bucksLeft/resolved/allResolved time-based; spawn log `this.log`; follow mode uses visible||entered||flee; finish('time') marks remaining bucks escaped/lost.\n   - src/92-hunt.js: Hunt.setupLens(); initial cam at establish.to; G.talk.draw(r) after overlay; queues for range/bonusOnly/quick end with {kind:'next'}; hub mode ignores seg done (segDone); site closed guard; anyConfirm no longer excludes bots; DEV hooks; moCrash camera.\n   - src/95-attract.js: HunterBot with project() measuring screen velocity (svx/svy) and lead = S.smooth (0 for cheat); cheat snaps reticle; tol = max(S.tol, zonePx*.7); `p.rifle.infinite = H.mode !== 'range'`; Duke calling; ATTRACT playlist; attractScene; G.lodge = G.lodge || new Lodge().\n   - src/96-dev.js: DEV.open does `G.ui.hide(); if (game.paused) game.resume(); ... game.after(0, () => this.show()); this.show();`.\n   - src/97-hub.js: HubLink with segAt/goSeg/catch-up, card input (confirm/start/fire → ready; call/more → more), sendResult once, end mutes; SEG.hubFinal; hubScene; drawHubCard.\n   - src/90-title.js: Idle clears touchOnly only `if (G.touchOnly && I.anyPressed() && I.lastDevice !== 'touch')`.\n   - src/52-glyphs.js: mousemove (with movement, non-touch) sets `Glyph.mouseUsed = true` and `G.game.input.lastDevice = 'mouse'`.\n   - src/81-bugle.js: knoll plateau z [520,455,7]; rim plateau z [565,560,6]; talus mark bit 32 → talus/rock types; valley depth 14 width 60; ridge height 16; brighter sun/ambient; goldgrass thinner fanP .5; trap house moved to (600,822) yaw 62 with props near; Duke calls:5, rules.update camera toward opening.\n   - src/80-hollow.js, 82-muskeg.js: fovs ×0.8, follow at 12 s, fanP scatter rules, leaves amount .1, iron-rack fog with fill.\n   - build/lib.mjs, build/manifest.json, build/build.mjs (lints for TODO/FIXME/XXX/placeholder/lorem, network/popups, Math.random; metas; session client first/hash; writes exit-interview.json from report.json validating shape).\n   - report.json: current values (testing/usage \"unknown\", all feedback \"unknown\") — must be updated with real feedback, testing description, then rebuild.\n   - tests/: lib/load.mjs, lib/t.mjs, lib/play.mjs (startSite step(.5)), lib/hubstub.mjs (progressLog), run.mjs, unit.test.mjs, flow-sites-*.test.mjs, flow-playthrough.test.mjs, flow-modes.test.mjs, flow-misc.test.mjs, flow-hub.test.mjs, browser/checks.mjs (deep links, pick check with per-animal stats & antler-skip for outside, touch, glyphs); scratch scripts (gallery.mjs, play.mjs, shot.mjs, botdbg, duke, bonusdbg, rangedbg, range5, pickdbg, pickimg, devopen, smoke).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Generation slow (3.2s→1.4s): coarse-grid Catmull-Rom noise fields, chamfer water distance on 2-sample grid, inline segDist + coarse path fields for wide features, forest computed once before types.\n   - Headless render crash (ccol null) → default colours.\n   - Lint false positives: `Glyph.prompt` method → renamed `Glyph.cue`; babble comment \"Math.random (\" reworded; HUD icon state 'todo' → 'ahead'.\n   - SEG TDZ → moved `const SEG = {}` to 00-core.\n   - Hunt class not hoisted for trophy hook → trophyCamStep/trophyCamView called from Hunt.\n   - Deep link not firing headless (promise) → call link() synchronously when headless.\n   - Lens only set in draw (headless visibility wrong) → setupLens in update and draw.\n   - Bot never killed running bucks → cheat snap, screen-velocity lead, zone-size tolerance; follow camera tracked only visible bucks → entered/flee too.\n   - Time-up bucks not counted escaped → finish('time') marks them.\n   - Dialog/skip ignored while bot played → removed `!p.bot`.\n   - Duke never heard calls when hidden; 2 calls insufficient → trophy rules first, calls:5; camera toward openings.\n   - Range: cheat infinite ammo blocked pump station; near berm blocked 150 m lane → lowberm.\n   - Missing {kind:'next'} in bonusOnly/quick/range queues.\n   - Hub copies spawn drift (game.script vs catch-up steps, hit-stop) → site-clock scripts, no freeze in hub; stub progress bug fixed.\n   - Dev screen swept away with pause screen → hide then show.\n   - Free cam test blocked by open dev screen → test hides UI first.\n   - Touch-only cleared by tap → only action presses clear.\n   - Saves headless memory-only → test saves within same session.\n   - Pick test bug (skipTo current site killed segment) → wait for site; actors teleported with legs planted at origin → snapRig; zones too small → added body ellipsoids, legs, neck, head, ears, tail, pad.\n   - Dialog box never drawn in hunts → G.talk.draw(r); camera at map corner pre-dialog → init cam at establish.to; fog bank showing sky → fog.fill.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Solved: full campaign playthrough passes (title→menu→3 hunts→ceremony→about→title in ~28 s); all sites cleared by cheat bot; bonus/range/party/quick/single modes; attract/dev/touch/saves/determinism; hub stub flow. Visual iteration on Hollow (good), Bugle (reworked), Muskeg (good; burn snags thinned). Ongoing: browser pick-agreement check at 203/224 = 90.6% inside (needs ≥95%); outside now 10/220 (passes). Per-animal: buck d30 rel120 65/75, doe d37 67/75, buck d49 71/74. Debug image of buck at [-20,30] heading rel+120° showed lower legs all missed although drawn vs projected knee/hoof positions match within ~0.5 px (e.g. \"knee drawn 280.3,239.8 zone 280.3,240.0 | hoof drawn 280.9,248.4 zone 280.9,248.7\"). Next suspicion: rays near hooves hit ground first (resolveRay terrain check) or lower-leg radii too small vs drawn width — needs investigation (pickimg doesn't exclude terrain-occluded pixels; the checks test does).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - `/goal` command with args: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\"\n   - Twice: \"The user hasn't heard from you in a while — say in a few words what you're doing, then continue.\" (answered with short status updates)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Finish pick-agreement (WYSIWYG) browser check to ≥95% inside / ≤5% outside.\n   - Write AI Hub harness test (tests/hub/harness.mjs): copy harness.html/bridge.js/round.js + bundle into tests/out/hub, start `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, record PID/port, confirm page title \"Big Buck Hunt-Off\", run players=2&auto=1, players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1, scenario=host-leave; require window.__hubCheck.pass; stop server by PID only. Wire into run.mjs --hub (currently references 'hub/harness.mjs').\n   - Visual polish passes (title, menu, lodge, about, range, rock foreground ledge looks like flat grey band, tally head card spacing, Bugle Duke/timber view check), maybe balance (average bot strong).\n   - Rerun full `node tests/run.mjs` (and --browser) after changes.\n   - Fill report.json: sourceInformation.testing (allowed + what ran and results, harness result), usage (\"unknown\" unless estimate), and all feedback answers (testing counts of issues caught, critical ones, most/least helpful tests; engine likes/stuck/built/hardest/changes (glyph default, Shell rows/hidden, audio.bus, new modules vista/quadruped/babble)/one change; prompt feedback); verify online field mentions harness result; rebuild; verify exit-interview.json parses.\n   - Final chat reply containing Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections (same text as About screen/report.json).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Debugging the browser pick-agreement check. Last run of tests/browser/checks.mjs: \"FAIL pick: rays inside the drawn silhouettes hit the animal (>= 95%) {\"ins\":224,\"insHit\":203,\"outs\":220,\"outHit\":10,...,\"per\":[\"doe d36 rel127 0/0\",\"fawn d36 rel129 0/0\",\"buck d30 rel120 65/75\",\"doe d37 rel92 67/75\",\"buck d21 rel78 0/0\",\"buck d49 rel106 71/74\"]}\" and outside check passing. Then tests/scratch/pickimg.mjs (buck spawned at [-20, 30], heading set to atan2(to animal)+120°, other actors gone, props hidden) rendered tests/out/pick-debug.png showing lower legs below the knee all red (missed), with the printout showing drawn and projected knee/hoof positions match. The next step was to determine why rays over the lower legs miss despite matching positions (likely terrain hit first in resolveRay near the ground, or lower-leg zone radius vs drawn width).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue the pick-agreement investigation: in tests/scratch/pickimg.mjs, for the missed lower-leg pixels log `resolveRay` result kind/t versus the leg zone t (e.g., whether R.kind === 'ground' with t less than the animal's), then fix accordingly (e.g., in resolveRay let animal zones win over terrain hits within a small distance, or widen lower-leg radii to the drawn width `max(.5px, legR*k)`), rebuild, and rerun `TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp node tests/browser/checks.mjs` until inside ≥95% and outside ≤5%; then rerun the full headless suite `node tests/run.mjs`, then proceed to the hub harness test and the report/exit-interview/final reply.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build--20261104-050516--x4cdb93-work/8fb56c77-99e2-4018-a816-6b0a42973b6b.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8fb56c77-99e2-4018-a816-6b0a42973b6b","uuid":"28bd4a91-3398-4471-8555-df293c97c991","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:20:31.676Z","isSynthetic":true}
