{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011eM7HiSknWUjUgfBFvvJDm","type":"tool_result","content":"// 94-about: About & Credits: Source Information, the Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback (the same words as the chat\n// reply and exit-interview.json: the build puts report.json in as __REPORT__), and the credits. One idea a page, big text;\n// left and right (or L1 and R1, Q and E, a click on the arrows) turn the pages; back leaves.\nconst QUESTIONS = {\n  testingFeedback: ['How many issues did testing catch?', 'How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?', 'What was the most helpful test you ran?', 'What was the least helpful test you ran?'],\n  engineFeedback: ['What did you like most about the engine?', 'Did you get stuck or guess wrong?', 'What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?', 'What was the hardest part about using the engine?', 'What did you change in the engine, and why?', 'If you could change one thing about\n  promptFeedback: ['What did you like most about this prompt?', 'What was confusing?', 'What was the hardest thing to do?', 'What would you change in this prompt?']\n};\nconst SI_LABELS = [['date', 'Date'], ['source', 'Source'], ['plan', 'Plan'], ['genre', 'Genre'], ['perspective', 'Perspective'], ['tech', 'Tech'], ['artDirection', 'Art direction'], ['animation', 'Animation'], ['audio', 'Audio'], ['online', 'Online'], ['testing', 'Testing'], ['research', 'Research']\nfunction aboutPages() {\n  const R = __REPORT__ || {}, SI = R.sourceInformation || {}, pages = [];\n  // Source Information: a few fields a page, so every word stays big\n  const fields = SI_LABELS.map(([k, l]) => [l, SI[k] || 'unknown']);\n  for (let i = 0; i < fields.length; i += 3) pages.push({ title: 'SOURCE INFORMATION', items: fields.slice(i, i + 3) });\n  for (const [key, title] of [['testingFeedback', 'TESTING FEEDBACK'], ['engineFeedback', 'ENGINE FEEDBACK'], ['promptFeedback', 'PROMPT FEEDBACK']]) {\n    const A = R[key] || []; QUESTIONS[key].forEach((q, i) => pages.push({ title, items: [[q, A[i] || 'unknown']] }));\n  }\n  pages.push({ title: 'CREDITS', items: [['Game', 'BIG BUCK HUNT-OFF. Design, code, pixels and sound made in code by Claude (Anthropic claude-opus-5-5), from a plan by claude-opus-5-5.'], ['Engine', 'my-3D2dge v0.85.2 by Michael Crosato (MIT). New modules: vista (the landscape), quadruped (animals a\n  pages.push({ title: 'CREDITS', items: [['Sound', 'Every song, sound and voice is synthesized in code: no audio files.'], ['Assets', 'Furniture shapes from the engine\\'s core library. Trees, rocks, corn, reeds and buildings painted in code for this game.'], ['The cast', 'Uncle Dub, Granny Mae, Cous\n  pages.push({ title: 'CREDITS', items: [['Inspired by', 'Big Buck Hunter Pro (Play Mechanix / Raw Thrills, 2006). An original game: its own title, people, places, bonus games, writing, art and sound.'], ['Thanks', 'To every hunter who ever pumped a plastic shotgun at a bar. Bucks only!']] });\n  return pages;\n}\nconst aboutScene = {\n  camera: { zoom: false }, touch: [],\n  enter(o = {}) { G.scene = 'about'; this.pages = aboutPages(); this.i = o.credits ? this.pages.findIndex(p => p.title === 'CREDITS') : 0; this.t = 0; if (G.sfx) G.sfx.music('lodgefire', { fade: .6 }); },\n  update(dt) {\n    this.t += dt; showcase().update(dt); if (G.sfx) G.sfx.update(dt); if (G.ui.screen) return;\n    const turn = d => { const j = clamp(this.i + d, 0, this.pages.length - 1); if (j !== this.i) { this.i = j; UISND.focus(); } };\n    if (uiRepeat('right') || uiPressed('tabR')) turn(1); if (uiRepeat('left') || uiPressed('tabL')) turn(-1);\n    const c = G.game.input.clicked && G.game.input.clicked(); if (c && this.arrows) { if (c[0] < this.arrows[0]) turn(-1); else if (c[0] > this.arrows[1]) turn(1); }\n59:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n60-- Date: 2026-11-04 05:05:16\n61-- Source: the work it's based on\n62-- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n63-- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n64-- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n65-- Art Direction: style used\n66-- Animation: system used\n67-- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n68-- Online: network features used, or none\n69-- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n70-- Research: research done, or none\n71-- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n72-- Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\n73-- Usage: the estimated API cost in USD, total number of tokens in K or M (provide break down if available) and session time, only if estimates are available.\n74-\n75-Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n76-{\n77-  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"\"},\n78:  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n79-  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n80-  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n81-  \"aiHub\": {\n82-    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n83-    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n84-    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\